message: "If you use SynthAudit, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "SynthAudit: Reference-Free Auditing of Synthetic Datasets for Generator Artifacts Before Machine Learning"
authors:
  - family-names: Erwin
    given-names: Randy
    email: erwinrandy3@gmail.com
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-23
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/rvndye/synthaudit"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/synthaudit/"
url: "https://rvndye.github.io/synthaudit/"
keywords:
  - synthetic data
  - data leakage
  - benchmark validity
  - dataset auditing
  - causal discovery
  - data-centric AI
abstract: >-
  SynthAudit audits released synthetic and simulated tabular datasets for
  generator artifacts before machine learning: exact and near-exact
  identities, rule- and threshold-derived labels, functional dependencies,
  schedule leakage, and train/test contamination. It classifies every column,
  separates benchmark leakage from legitimate structural constraints, and
  aggregates the evidence into a decomposable Benchmark Trustworthiness
  Index. A methodology paper is under submission; this file will be updated
  with the preferred citation on acceptance.
